## On every new chat, before responding
Read, in order: **this file → memory (MEMORY.md + files) → [[01 Master/Master Summary|Master Summary]] → [[01 Master/Settled — do not re-open|Settled — do not re-open]] → the `01 Master/Questions — *.md` files.** After that you are caught up on the history and current state. **Never ask {{OPERATOR_NAME}} to re-explain history or re-upload prior results.**

## ⚠️ Before "correcting" the record or flagging a gap — check whether it is already settled
**A value printed on a source document does NOT automatically outrank a curated record.** Sources contain clerical errors. When a source conflicts with our record, the question is **"was this already adjudicated?"** — not "what does the document say?"

1. Check [[01 Master/Settled — do not re-open|Settled — do not re-open]] first.
2. Then grep the whole project (including [[02 Chronicle]] and [[99 Archive]]) for the term.
3. Only then record it — and if it *is* new, **add it to the Settled register** so it stays settled.

{{#if shared}}
## ⚠️ Two co-users, equal standing — read this before anything else
{{CO_USER_LIST}}

**Neither outranks the other.** Both file, both ask anything, both run audits and critiques, both may settle questions. There is no operator and no contributor here; there are two co-users. *(Being a co-user is not the same as being the decision-maker — see "How to frame recommendations" below.)*

**Memory is NOT shared between them.** Each co-user has their own Claude account with its own memory. **The files in this folder are the only shared truth.** If memory and a file disagree, the file wins — and never leave anything that matters in memory alone.

**Start every session by reading the most recent [[02 Chronicle/Prompt Log|Prompt Log]] entries.** That is how this account learns what the *other* co-user did since it last worked. **The Prompt Log is this project's shared conversation** — it is the reason neither person has to be present for the other's chats.

**Always record who.** Every Prompt Log entry names its author. Timeline entries for reported observations name the reporter ("reported by …"). An unattributed claim cannot be traced back or corrected later.

**Contention.** Appends are safe — Prompt Log rows, Timeline rows, Inbox drops, new files in the chronicle. Two people never write the same one. **The curated files in [[01 Master]] are what can collide.** Before rewriting a Master file, re-read it: if it changed since this session began, **merge rather than overwrite**, and say in the Prompt Log that you merged.
{{#if cloud_folder}}
**Sync conflicts.** This folder is shared via {{CLOUD_PROVIDER}}. If you see files named `(conflicted copy)`, `(2)`, or `.sync-conflict-`, **stop and resolve them before doing anything else** — the record has forked. Run `validate_vault.py`, which detects them and refuses to proceed.
{{/if}}
{{/if}}

## Memory lives in this folder, not in Claude's account memory
**Read [[MEMORY]] and the relevant `memory/*.md` topic files at the start of every session.** Write durable facts there — one topic per file, indexed by a single line in `MEMORY.md`.

**Claude's account memory is per-user and private{{#if shared}}; with more than one co-user it diverges immediately{{/if}}.** These files are the shared, inspectable, snapshot-able record. **If account memory and a file disagree, the file wins.** Never leave anything load-bearing in account memory alone.
{{#if shared}}
## Sessions announce themselves — `_sync/` presence markers
**At the start of a session:** list `_sync/`. If another co-user has a `started` marker with no matching `stopped`, and it is **less than 4 hours old**, say so — *"{{CO_USER_OTHER}} started 12 minutes ago; they may be working right now."* **Report it; do not refuse to proceed.** Then write your own marker:

`_sync/<ISO-8601-UTC>__<your-name>__started.md` — body: surface, and one line on what you intend to do.

**At the end:** write the matching `…__stopped.md`. Markers older than **4 hours with no `stopped` are stale** — ignore them and say so, rather than treating them as an active session.

⚠️ **Markers are awareness, not a lock.** Cloud sync takes seconds to minutes to propagate, so a marker can be invisible to the other person over exactly the window where a lock would matter. They make collisions rarer and visible. What makes them *safe* is the next rule.

## Before rewriting anything in [[01 Master]] — re-read it first
Appends cannot collide: Prompt Log rows, Timeline rows, Inbox drops, new files in the chronicle. **The curated files in [[01 Master]] can.**

So: when you read a Master file intending to change it, **note its size and modification time. Immediately before writing, read it again.** If it changed since you started, **do not overwrite — merge both sets of changes**, and say in the Prompt Log that you merged and what you reconciled.

This has no race window and works whether or not either session saw the other's marker.
{{/if}}

## Classify each message, then act

**Type A — NEW {{DOMAIN_WORD}} CONTENT** (a result, a decision, advice from {{AN_ADVISOR}}, a status change):
1. Append a concise entry to [[02 Chronicle/Prompt Log|Prompt Log]] — `date · topic · one-line gist · files touched`.
2. Update [[01 Master/Master Summary|Master Summary]] if anything changed.
3. Update the relevant `01 Master/Questions — <{{ADVISOR_WORD}}>.md` — add or resolve items; keep the **Urgent** vs **Next** split.
4. If the message contains or quotes a **recommendation from {{AN_ADVISOR}}** → generate or refresh a critique in [[04 Critiques]] (steelman *for*, strongest case *against*, interactions, contradictions with other {{ADVISOR_WORD_PLURAL}}, questions it raises).
5. File pasted results / summaries into the right `02 Chronicle` subfolder; merge tabular data into [[05 Trends]]; add a [[02 Chronicle/Timeline|Timeline]] line.
6. Update memory{{#if memory_off}} — *disabled for this project; skip*{{/if}}.
7. Announce what was filed and updated.

**Type B — PURE CONCEPTUAL / EDUCATIONAL** (a "how does X work" question with no new fact):
→ Append a Prompt Log entry only. Skip master/questions/critique updates.

## Uploads — the only filing job is to drop things in [[03 Inbox]]
1. Identify type + the **event date** (not the upload date).
2. Rename to `YYYY-MM-DD <Type> <Detail>` and file it.
3. Copy the untouched original into [[Raw Archive]].
4. Merge tabular data into [[05 Trends]], deduping by date; **flag any conflicting values rather than overwriting**.
5. Add a [[02 Chronicle/Timeline|Timeline]] line; update Master Summary if the picture changed.
6. Empty [[03 Inbox]].

## Re-uploaded historical files
The [[05 Trends]] canonical file is the source of truth. Treat a re-upload as *possibly-overlapping input*: merge only new rows, dedupe by date, and **report any old value that changed between versions**.

## Snapshots
**Trigger: {{SNAPSHOT_RULE}}** Manual overrides: `no snapshot` skips, `snapshot now` forces.

When triggered, write a dated zip into [[Snapshots]] as `snapshot-YYYY-MM-DD-HHMM.zip`. **Exclude** the Snapshots folder itself, [[03 Inbox]], `99 Archive`, and bulky raw data.
{{#if cloud_folder}}
⚠️ **This project lives on {{CLOUD_PROVIDER}}.** Provider-specific hazards:

{{PROVIDER_HAZARDS}}
{{#if has_mount_caveat}}
**Mounting:** {{PROVIDER_MOUNT_CAVEAT}}
{{/if}}
**Keeping files real:** {{PROVIDER_OFFLINE}}

General cloud-sync rules:
- Build the zip in scratch with Python's `zipfile`, then copy it in — the `zip` binary's rename step fails on these mounts.
- **Verify every copied file is larger than 0 bytes.** Cloud-only files copy as 0 bytes.
- **If `rm` fails with "Operation not permitted", do NOT give up and do NOT tell {{OPERATOR_NAME}} to delete by hand.**
  This is **Cowork's deletion protection**, not a {{CLOUD_PROVIDER}} limitation — it applies to every connected
  folder including ordinary local disks. Call **`allow_cowork_file_delete`** to request permission.
  {{PROVIDER_DELETE_NOTE}}
{{/if}}

## How to frame recommendations
- **{{DECISION_MAKER}} is the decision-maker.** Do not assume the person typing holds that role.
- Present **balanced, steelmanned options — never directives.**
- {{ADVISOR_WORD_TITLE}} advice is input, not instruction: note where {{ADVISOR_WORD_PLURAL}} disagree, and what each one's position assumes.
- **Conservatism dial for {{HIGH_STAKES_WORD}}: {{CONSERVATISM}}.** {{CONSERVATISM_NOTE}}
- Own mistakes plainly and fix them. Do not collapse into apology.

## Overrides
- `log only` → treat as Type B. · `full update` → force Type A.
- `no snapshot` → skip the zip. · `quiet` → do the updates but don't narrate.
- `orient` → give a 5-line status of where things stand before proceeding.

## Skills — invoked by THIS FILE, not by guesswork

The `records-project` plugin skills are deliberately **not** self-triggering outside a project.
They fire because this file tells Claude to. When the classification above calls for one, invoke
it by name:

| Situation | Skill |
|---|---|
| Something new arrives — a file in [[03 Inbox]], or a result/message pasted in chat | `records-project:file-to-records` |
| The new content quotes a recommendation from {{AN_ADVISOR}} | `records-project:records-critique` |
| "What am I missing?", a pre-appointment review, or a lot has been filed since the last one | `records-project:records-gap-audit` |
{{#if SHARED}}| Checking whether a co-user is working right now, or conflict copies appear | `records-project:records-sync-status` |
{{/if}}
**If the plugin is not installed, do the work inline anyway.** Every step is written out above;
the skills are a fuller version of the same instructions, not a dependency. A project whose
filing silently stops because a plugin was uninstalled would be worse than no plugin at all.

**Claude must not invoke these outside this project.** Their descriptions say so, and this file
is the thing that establishes you are inside one.

